REM A starter task for capturing a system snapshot. Curated example.
REM Copy this to ~/.caro/library/system/snapshot.caro for personal use.

TASK Capture a quick system snapshot
WHY  Trace a moment in time before/after risky operations; doubles as a sanity probe.

ON   macos PREFER bsd-tools
ON   linux PREFER gnu-tools

LET  out = /tmp/caro-snapshot.txt

NOTE keep it terse; one line per fact, no shell loops
DO   record current date and hostname to {out}
DO   append uname -a output
DO   append disk usage of the user's home directory
DO   append the top 5 processes by RSS
DO   echo where the snapshot was written
